 About: GPU 0 · NVIDIA GeForce RTX 3080 Ti Laptop GPU                                               
   Utilization     How busy the GPU is: the busiest engine, as in Task Manager. Games show up as    
                   3D; AI and CUDA work as 3D or Compute. High utilization is normal while gaming   
                   or running a model.                                                              
   Engines         3D: games, the desktop, some AI. Compute: CUDA / AI work. Copy: moving data      
                   between RAM and the GPU, high while loading a game or model. Video Decode /      
                   Encode: watching, streaming or recording video, done by dedicated hardware.      
   Dedicated       The GPU's own memory (VRAM). A local LLM must fit here to run fast; when it's    
                   full, data spills into shared memory over PCIe and tokens per second drop        
                   sharply. Games stutter when they run out.                                        
   Shared          System RAM the GPU can borrow. Integrated GPUs use only this. On a discrete GPU, 
                   heavy use means VRAM has run out.                                                
   Temperature     GPU core temperature. 30–50 °C idle is normal; laptops often run 70–87 °C under  
                   load. Near the GPU's limit (about 87 °C for NVIDIA) clocks drop to cool down.    
   Power           Current power draw, and the limit when the driver reports one. On laptops the    
                   limit is set by the manufacturer and is often what caps performance.             
   Clock           Current vs maximum graphics clock. Low clocks while idle are normal; low clocks  
                   under load mean something is limiting the GPU (see Limited by).                  
   P-state         Performance state: P0 is full performance, higher numbers (P8, P12) are power-   
                   saving idle states.                                                              
   Limited by      Why clocks are below maximum right now. idle: nothing to do. power cap: hit the  
                   power limit (usual on laptops under load). thermal: too hot, so improve cooling. 
                   reliability: the driver is keeping voltage in a safe range (normal). hardware    
                   slowdown / power brake: an emergency limit, worth investigating.                 
                                                                                                    
